    <GaugingStation location="Clog-y-Fran" name="Taf" number="60003">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station. Natural flow regime. Station used for flood forecasting and drought trigger.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Left bank steep with berm for recorder - recent signs of erosion. Right flood bank at approx 3.2 - 3.4m; considerable overspill during flood events. Channel prone to build-up of silt. Gauged from bridge u/s which can also become constriction at high flows. Flood rating change in early 1990s; exact date of change is estimated. Rating fits gaugings reasonably and allowance is made for bypass flow. Remedial works to stabilise the riverbank downstream of the gauging station and the bank to the rear of the gauging station began in July 2022 and finished September 2022. During this time a temporary site, was positioned in the river channel using a stilling pipe approx. 30m upstream of the station.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity area station. Channel width: 13.9m. Site used for flood forecasting and drought trigger.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Flow record from 60002 Cothi at Felin Mynachdy used to infill various short periods of missing data (principally in 1986, but also 1991, 2001, 2004). Flows from 01/01/2010 reprocessed in 2013 due to new rating, with main effect of lowering low flow GDFs, and from 01/0/1982 in 2025. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Natural to within 10% at Q95.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Mainly impermeable strata, Ordovician with some narrow bands of igneous rock, Old Red Sandstone in S. Alluvium in valleys. Soils have permeable substrate. Largely grassland, mainly dairy farming. Very small patches of arable and woodland.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED. Rating accounts for some out of bank flow and is well gauged." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Gauged close to AMAX3 but there is limited confidence the rating accurately accounting for out of bank flow. Borderline suitable for Pooling." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
